# Normalize line endings across machines.
#
# Shell scripts and Docker entrypoints MUST stay LF. If they are checked out
# with CRLF (the Windows default when core.autocrlf=true), they break inside
# Linux containers — the kernel tries to run interpreter "/bin/sh\r", the
# container crashes on startup, and the API becomes unreachable
# (ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED). This is the #1 "works on one PC, fails on another"
# bug for Dockerized shell entrypoints.
* text=auto

*.sh            text eol=lf
docker-entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
